# Local research corpus and generated artifacts
data/
output/

# `evals/` is ignored because it holds 877MB of vendored upstream clones
# (topoteretes/cognee, C-Bjorn/MegaMem) carrying uncommitted local work that
# exists in no git repository — see the Testing section of AGENTS.md. Our own
# eval harnesses live alongside them and ARE project code.
#
# Written as `evals/*` plus negations rather than `evals/`: git cannot
# re-include anything beneath an excluded directory, so the contents have to be
# excluded individually for the negations to bind. The clones stay ignored
# because `evals/*` still matches them.
evals/*
!evals/__init__.py
!evals/metrics.py
!evals/federation/
!evals/growth/
!evals/qa/
!evals/lme_mab/
!evals/tck/

# Un-ignoring evals/qa/ re-exposes anything a run drops in it. The QA runner
# defaults --out to ~/.blackhole/ instead, so this only catches the operator who
# passes the in-repo path explicitly — but a comparative table naming a
# competitor is exactly the file that must never arrive via `git add -A`, and
# #178's _first_party_docs() does not scan evals/, so nothing else would see it.
evals/qa/report*.md
evals/qa/answers/

# But: the demo corpus under examples/ IS checked in.
!examples/demo-corpus/data/
!examples/demo-corpus/data/**

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# PyPI build artifacts (from `python -m build`)
dist/
build/

# pip transient scratch dirs that leak into cwd when a pip run is
# interrupted or TMPDIR resolves here. Normally auto-deleted under
# $TMPDIR; ignored so an interrupted install never clutters git.
pip-build-tracker-*/
pip-ephem-wheel-cache-*/
pip-install-*/
pip-unpack-*/
pip-build-env-*/
pip-metadata-*/
pip-modern-metadata-*/

# Local graph/database outputs
.tesserae/
.understand-anything/
*.sqlite
*.kuzu/
*.duckdb

# Local agent session markers
.agent-sessions/
# ...but the demo corpus ships hand-authored agent-session transcripts.
!examples/demo-corpus/.agent-sessions/
!examples/demo-corpus/.agent-sessions/**
.hermes/
.tesserae/external/raganything/working_dir/
.tesserae/external/raganything/parsed/

# pytest temp directories — created when tmp_path_factory points at the repo
pytest-of-*/
# ...and the bare mkdtemp() names some tests still use instead of tmp_path.
# `pytest-of-*/` never matched those, so fleet/daemon scratch kept landing in
# the repo root as untracked dirs — one `git add -A` away from being committed,
# and enough to block a release pre-flight on a dirty tree.
tmp??????*/
node-compile-cache/

# Local IDE / AI-assistant configs — per-developer, do not commit
.agents/
.aider.conf.yml
.aider*
.avante/
# `.claude/` is per-developer EXCEPT skills/, which are project procedure —
# the release flow, the UI-verification loop. Keeping those untracked meant a
# release procedure that existed on exactly one laptop, which is the same class
# of problem as a test suite that only passes on one laptop.
#
# Written as `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`: git cannot re-include anything
# under a directory that is itself excluded, so the negation below only works
# if the contents are excluded individually.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.clinerules
.cline/
.codecompanion/
.codex/
.continue/
.cursor/
.gemini/
.harness-sync/
.opencode/
.playwright-mcp/
.roo/
.zed/

# AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md are TRACKED. They are project convention — the
# mission statement, the CodeGraph and agentmemory usage rules, the testing
# invariants, the warning that evals/ holds unrecoverable local work. Every
# agent and every contributor needs them, and .github/copilot-instructions.md
# and .codeium/instructions.md already point at them.
#
# Keep them free of anything per-developer: no absolute home paths, no account
# names, no credentials. A machine-specific override belongs in a *.local.md
# beside them, not inline.
GEMINI.md
CONVENTIONS.md
SYNC-CHANGELOG.md
config.toml
opencode.json
data-gym-cache/

# uv lockfiles can vary by lockfile version + platform — keep out of tree
uv-*.lock

# grd evolve / autopilot planning artifacts — per-developer state
.planning/

# Local tool state / OS noise (never ship)
.DS_Store
.codegraph/
tsx-501/
graph-3d.png
